\ init.fam — the first program the kernel runs (docs/OS.md), in user mode.
\ It keeps a shell on the console: started, and started again when it ends.
\ (Step 8: what /etc/init lists.)

: st variable ;
"init: starting the shell" puts 0A lit putc
begin
	"sh" spawn dup 0< if "init: no shell: " puts . 0A lit putc 1 lit exit then
	st wait drop
	"init: the shell ended; again" puts 0A lit putc
0 lit until
